1
00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:20,285
They came for the gold. They stayed for the adventure.

2
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:34,571
The Road to El Dorado is a family, adventure,
animation film directed by Bibo Bergeron.

3
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
Stowing away after a failed con, a pair of swindlers end up on El Dorado, the fabled "city of gold", where
they quickly get in over their heads when they are mistaken as gods by the inhabitants.

4
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:03,142
Miguel  (voice), played by Kenneth Branagh.

5
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:17,428
Tulio (voice), played by Kevin Kline.

6
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Chel (voice), played by Rosie Perez.

7
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Tzekel-Kan (voice), played by Armand Assante.

8
00:33:54,285 --> 00:34:00,285
Chief (voice), played by Edward James Olmos.

9
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Cortes (voice), played by Jim Cummings.

10
00:42:22,857 --> 00:42:28,857
The Road to El Dorado is a 2000 American animated musical adventure comedy film directed by Eric "Bibo" Bergeron and Don Paul, from a
screenplay by Ted Elliott and Terry Rossio, as well as additional sequences directed by Will Finn and David Silverman.

11
00:46:37,142 --> 00:46:43,142
Starring the voices of Kevin Kline, Kenneth Branagh, Rosie Perez, Armand Assante, and Edward James Olmos, the film follows a pair of con artists who, after winning the
map to El Dorado in Spain, wash ashore in the New World; the map leads the two men to the city of El Dorado, where its inhabitants mistake them for gods.

12
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
The soundtrack features an instrumental score composed by Hans Zimmer and
John Powell, and songs written by Elton John and Tim Rice.

13
00:55:05,714 --> 00:55:11,714
John also periodically narrates the story in song throughout the film.

14
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
Produced by DreamWorks Animation and released by DreamWorks Pictures, it
was the third animated feature produced by the studio.

15
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
The Road to El Dorado was theatrically released in
the United States on March 31, 2000.

16
01:07:48,571 --> 01:07:54,571
It received mixed reviews from critics and underperformed at the box office, grossing $76
million worldwide on a production budget of approximately $95 million.

17
01:12:02,857 --> 01:12:08,857
Zimmer's work on the score, however, received praise and earned him the Critics' Choice Movie Award for Best
Score alongside his work on Gladiator, another DreamWorks film, at the 6th Critics' Choice Awards.

18
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
Despite its initial reception, reevaluation in later years has
resulted in The Road to El Dorado becoming a cult classic.

19
01:20:31,428 --> 01:20:37,428
The film explores themes of gold, horse, cartoon, musical, con artist.

20
01:24:45,714 --> 01:24:51,714
The tone is lighthearted.
